WEBVTT


WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:08.250
This sock is knit from
the heel up to the cuff.

2
00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:12.220
We'll start by working
an open caston for the heel.

3
00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:14.700
We'll be joining these open stitches

4
00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:21.140
to the leg later, so cast
on with waist yarn and ravel cord.

5
00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:26.620
Next, we'll start shaping
the heel with short row shaping.

6
00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:30.100
Set your carriage to hold
in both directions.

7
00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:35.220
Now, following the pattern on the carriage
side, I'm putting one needle into hold

8
00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:40.380
position and I'll knit across
again on the carriage side.

9
00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:44.060
Put a needle into hold
position and knit across.

10
00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:48.220
Now, this is automatic
wrap short row shaping.

11
00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:53.280
Just keep repeating this
according to your pattern.

12
00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:00.820
Now, if this shaping is new to you,

13
00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:06.130
please study the tutorials that are
included with this course.

14
00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:13.280
Also, please practice this technique
before you start knitting your socks.

15
00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:31.380
When the short rows decreases are
complete, I'll shortrow increase until all

16
00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:36.320
the needles are back
into working position.

17
00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:13.700
Now that the heel is finished,

18
00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:18.450
I'll knit the sole indicated
by the letter C on the diagram.

19
00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:22.600
This is the bottom of the foot.

20
00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:39.170
When that knitting is complete,
we'll knit the toe.

21
00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:42.060
Again, we're going to use
short row shaping.

22
00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:44.900
But this time, notice that I'm using.

23
00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:47.940
A manual wrap method.

24
00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:53.900
The needles are pulled out into hold
on the opposite side of the carriage,

25
00:02:53.930 --> 00:03:00.840
and then the yarn is manually
wrapped to prevent holes.

26
00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:12.820
These two methods are explored

27
00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:19.300
in a tutorial in this course under
the heel and toe technique section.

28
00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:25.380
Now, if all of this is new to you,
please watch, learn and practice both

29
00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:32.560
automatic and manual short rows
shaping and decide which you prefer.

30
00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:58.780
Now that the toe is done,
we'll knit the instep of the sock.

31
00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:06.800
This is a great place to get creative
with cables or lace or color work.

32
00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:13.860
In this example,
I put stripes on the instep only.

33
00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:19.680
It's a great way to incorporate
little bits of yarn.

34
00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:30.140
Now, here's the fun part.

35
00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:33.380
Remember those live stitches at the heel?

36
00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:39.980
We're going to turn the knitting so that
the pearl side of that heel is facing us.

37
00:04:40.010 --> 00:04:44.140
And then hang those live
stitches on the machine.

38
00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:48.260
Just take care that you
don't twist the sock.

39
00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:51.620
Take a minute to make sure

40
00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:54.980
you can rehang this, either on the left
or the right side of the work.

41
00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:57.720
It really doesn't matter.

42
00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:02.260
We're just joining the heel to the.

43
00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:06.640
Leg at this point, eliminating a seam.

44
00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:12.180
Now notice that I've doubled up
the seaming stitches at the join here.

45
00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:17.120
This will make seaming
neater at that join point.

46
00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:36.780
Once all the stitches are on the machine,

47
00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:41.460
continue to knit the leg in the stitch
pattern of your choice

48
00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:47.260
knitting pattern instructs you to knit
a few rows plain for a transition.

49
00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:53.700
And at that point, feel free to transfer
stitches to the river for a ribbed leg or

50
00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:55.820
remove the knitting
on hand knitting needles.

51
00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:59.200
To hand knit some ribbing.

52
00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:07.980
I chose to knit a plain
leg with a rolled edge.

53
00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:13.100
I worked the figure eight
bind off for lots of stitch.

54
00:06:13.130 --> 00:06:16.080
Except for the finishing my socks.
Done.

